(7380503, 1158732, 115814, '<td valign="top">I''m enjoying being part of the DPL <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1296711" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">First ten!</a> side challenge. Yours is photo #3 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge. <br/> <br/>Intriguing use of the rule here, with two separate attention points in diagonal opposition at the intersection points. It works on one level, but also creates an interesting tension between the cat''s eye and the flower. The front leg bridges the gap as a leading line, but it still feels visually unsettled to me. The exposure and background are exceptional.</td>', 'I''m enjoying being part of the DPL First ten! side challenge. Yours is photo #3 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge.  Intriguing use of the rule here, with two separate attention points in diagonal opposition at the intersection points. It works on one level, but also creates an interesting tension between the cat''s eye and the flower. The front leg bridges the gap as a leading line, but it still feels visually unsettled to me. The exposure and background are exceptional.', '2015-07-02 16:50:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(7380504, 1158524, 115814, '<td valign="top">I''m enjoying being part of the DPL <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1296711" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">First ten!</a> side challenge. Yours is photo #8 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge. <br/> <br/>A truly captivating image. Shadow and girl created a horizontal division of three, with dappled, rippled light in between. Definitely got my attention in a good way.</td>', 'I''m enjoying being part of the DPL First ten! side challenge. Yours is photo #8 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge.  A truly captivating image. Shadow and girl created a horizontal division of three, with dappled, rippled light in between. Definitely got my attention in a good way.', '2015-07-02 16:50:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7380505, 1158855, 115814, '<td valign="top">I''m enjoying being part of the DPL <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1296711" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">First ten!</a> side challenge. Yours is photo #10 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge. <br/> <br/>Very interesting shot, with a sense of abstraction and concrete at the same time. The patterns on the wall immediately caught my attention in a good way. The emphasis of the bright white areas brings attention to the right side and specifically the boulder. Then... the bird appears from out of the background and its placement by the rule of thirds locks it in as the primary subject. Fascinating eye movement getting from the reveal to the bird. Cool.</td>', 'I''m enjoying being part of the DPL First ten! side challenge. Yours is photo #10 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge.  Very interesting shot, with a sense of abstraction and concrete at the same time. The patterns on the wall immediately caught my attention in a good way. The emphasis of the bright white areas brings attention to the right side and specifically the boulder. Then... the bird appears from out of the background and its placement by the rule of thirds locks it in as the primary subject. Fascinating eye movement getting from the reveal to the bird. Cool.', '2015-07-02 16:50:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(7380508, 1158771, 115814, '<td valign="top">I''m enjoying being part of the DPL <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1296711" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">First ten!</a> side challenge. Yours is photo #1 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge. <br/> <br/>Follows the rule as far as I can see. Eyes are tack sharp, and shallow DOF works to isolate part of the subject. Nice bokeh and colors. Wish the abdomen and thorax were better in focus, but hard to do in macro without focus-stacking.</td>', 'I''m enjoying being part of the DPL First ten! side challenge. Yours is photo #1 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge.  Follows the rule as far as I can see. Eyes are tack sharp, and shallow DOF works to isolate part of the subject. Nice bokeh and colors. Wish the abdomen and thorax were better in focus, but hard to do in macro without focus-stacking.', '2015-07-02 16:55:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(7380509, 1157332, 115814, '<td valign="top">I''m enjoying being part of the DPL <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1296711" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">First ten!</a> side challenge. Yours is photo #2 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge. <br/> <br/>Obviously following the rule here, which works to bring my attention to the center circle. Unfortunately, the focus and exposure at that spot aren''t as good as other parts of the image.</td>', 'I''m enjoying being part of the DPL First ten! side challenge. Yours is photo #2 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge.  Obviously following the rule here, which works to bring my attention to the center circle. Unfortunately, the focus and exposure at that spot aren''t as good as other parts of the image.', '2015-07-02 16:55:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(7380510, 1158256, 115814, '<td valign="top">I''m enjoying being part of the DPL <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1296711" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">First ten!</a> side challenge. Yours is photo #4 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge. <br/> <br/>A good example of using the rule of thirds. The sailboat immediately stands out as the focal point. But, the scale of the boat compared to the cave may confuse the issue of which subject is intended to dominate. What a great looking location, though. Makes me want to be in the boat.</td>', 'I''m enjoying being part of the DPL First ten! side challenge. Yours is photo #4 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge.  A good example of using the rule of thirds. The sailboat immediately stands out as the focal point. But, the scale of the boat compared to the cave may confuse the issue of which subject is intended to dominate. What a great looking location, though. Makes me want to be in the boat.', '2015-07-02 16:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(7380511, 1158393, 115814, '<td valign="top">I''m enjoying being part of the DPL <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1296711" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">First ten!</a> side challenge. Yours is photo #5 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge. <br/> <br/>The subject is so big relative to the frame that it''s hard for me to see how the rule is applied here. I think it might be more effective moving a step or two back to create more breathing room at bottom, left, and top. There''s also some distraction in the changing colors  (shades of green, redish brown, white) in the background.</td>', 'I''m enjoying being part of the DPL First ten! side challenge. Yours is photo #5 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge.  The subject is so big relative to the frame that it''s hard for me to see how the rule is applied here. I think it might be more effective moving a step or two back to create more breathing room at bottom, left, and top. There''s also some distraction in the changing colors  (shades of green, redish brown, white) in the background.', '2015-07-02 16:56:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(7380512, 1158484, 115814, '<td valign="top">I''m enjoying being part of the DPL <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1296711" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">First ten!</a> side challenge. Yours is photo #6 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge. <br/> <br/>So, I''m wondering if the main bubble/subject is the first to leave, or last to arrive? Can''t get more Rule of Third-y than this. Good lighting, focus, exposure (perhaps too bright on the lower right?)  and a consistent effective color palette.</td>', 'I''m enjoying being part of the DPL First ten! side challenge. Yours is photo #6 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge.  So, I''m wondering if the main bubble/subject is the first to leave, or last to arrive? Can''t get more Rule of Third-y than this. Good lighting, focus, exposure (perhaps too bright on the lower right?)  and a consistent effective color palette.', '2015-07-02 16:56:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(7380513, 1158741, 115814, '<td valign="top">I''m enjoying being part of the DPL <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1296711" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">First ten!</a> side challenge. Yours is photo #7 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge. <br/> <br/>Nicely framed by the natural elements. For me, there''s tension between the relative small size of the subject(s) and the massive tree framing the scene. Frankly, the tree wins for my attention, despite the human subject''s placement using the rule of thirds.</td>', 'I''m enjoying being part of the DPL First ten! side challenge. Yours is photo #7 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge.  Nicely framed by the natural elements. For me, there''s tension between the relative small size of the subject(s) and the massive tree framing the scene. Frankly, the tree wins for my attention, despite the human subject''s placement using the rule of thirds.', '2015-07-02 16:56:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(7380514, 1157682, 115814, '<td valign="top">I''m enjoying being part of the DPL <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1296711" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">First ten!</a> side challenge. Yours is photo #9 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge. <br/> <br/>Yep, the subjects are at the right place to satisfy the rule. While I''m curious about what''s got their attention out of frame on the left, I''m distracted by the mass of white featureless sky.</td>', 'I''m enjoying being part of the DPL First ten! side challenge. Yours is photo #9 in my random voting stream for the Rule of Thirds VI challenge.  Yep, the subjects are at the right place to satisfy the rule. While I''m curious about what''s got their attention out of frame on the left, I''m distracted by the mass of white featureless sky.', '2015-07-02 16:56:10.000000', NULL, 1),
