(7383902, 1158272, 94815, '<td valign="top">This is my favorite of the challenge. But, alas, it, too, like the vast majority, misses the "rule" and its importance. To my eye, the main element is the mouth, as it were, eating the spaghetti. So, for maximum impact, it should fall on the lower thirds hot spot but misses the intersection. The solution is so easy too. Simply crop off the image bottom up to the intersection of the line (piece of spaghetti) with the left edge of the frame. Try it and sit back and marvel at the difference.</td>', 'This is my favorite of the challenge. But, alas, it, too, like the vast majority, misses the "rule" and its importance. To my eye, the main element is the mouth, as it were, eating the spaghetti. So, for maximum impact, it should fall on the lower thirds hot spot but misses the intersection. The solution is so easy too. Simply crop off the image bottom up to the intersection of the line (piece of spaghetti) with the left edge of the frame. Try it and sit back and marvel at the difference.', '2015-07-08 00:29:41.000000', NULL, 1),
